        "event": "Special Weather Statement",
        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued September 28 at 2:42PM AKDT by NWS Fairbanks AK",
        "description": "Light rain and snow will meander around the Interior. Locations\nabove 2000ft have the highest chance for snow through Monday\nnight but snow levels continue to drop to 1000ft Tuesday. Valley\nlocations, including Fairbanks, may see some snowflakes mix in\nwith rain beginning Tuesday night with flurries lingering into\nWednesday. Little to no accumulation is expected in the valleys\nthrough Wednesday afternoon. Between 1000-2000ft, up to 1 inch of\nsnow is possible but there will be melting as the snow",
